Let a paletted platform have Doom draw straight into its frame buffer.

- SCREENPITCH (i_video.h, default SCREENWIDTH): bytes between rows of
  I_VideoBuffer. Everything that writes I_VideoBuffer uses it: the column
  drawers and row table (r_draw.c), V_* when drawing to the screen
  (v_video.c; other buffers stay SCREENWIDTH wide), automap, finale text
  and bunny scroll, R_VideoErase, I_ReadScreen, screenshots. The wipes work
  in a packed buffer and copy it out each step when the pitch differs.
- DG_DIRECT (doomgeneric.h): I_VideoBuffer comes from DG_VideoBuffer(),
  I_FinishUpdate only calls DG_DrawFrame, no DG_ScreenBuffer is allocated.
  With CMAP256 the platform reads colors[] when palette_changed is set.
  I_InitGraphics no longer prints doomgeneric's own 640x400 frame buffer
  and scaling factor, which a DG_DIRECT platform does not use.

Default builds (neither defined) behave as before.


